---
description: Control and document third-party data sharing in compliance with GDPR
alwaysApply: true
---

third-party-sharing:

- Obtain explicit consent before sharing data with third parties
- Maintain data processing agreements (DPAs) with all processors
- Document all third-party data transfers
- Implement data transfer impact assessments for international transfers
- Use Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) for non-EU transfers
- Provide transparency about third-party sharing in privacy policy
- Implement data sharing audit logs
- Verify third-party GDPR compliance

Requirements for third-party sharing:
- Legal basis for sharing (consent, contract, legitimate interest)
- Data Processing Agreement in place
- Privacy impact assessment completed
- User notification and consent
- Adequate safeguards for international transfers
- Right to object to sharing

Good implementation:
```javascript
// Check consent before sharing
async function shareWithThirdParty(userId, thirdParty, data) {
  const consent = await db.consents.findOne({
    userId,
    thirdParty,
    type: 'data-sharing'
  });
  
  if (!consent || !consent.granted) {
    throw new Error('No consent for third-party sharing');
  }
  
  // Log the transfer
  await db.dataTransfers.create({
    userId,
    thirdParty,
    dataTypes: Object.keys(data),
    timestamp: new Date(),
    legalBasis: 'consent'
  });
  
  return await thirdParty.api.send(data);
}
```

Bad practices:
```javascript
// Share without consent
await analytics.track(user.email, user.behavior);

// No documentation
await thirdPartyApi.send(userData); // No audit trail

// International transfer without safeguards
await usServer.store(euUserData); // GDPR violation
```
